# Customize the Text Reports

The layout of every report is fixed, but its texts come from a resource bundle that you can override.
Put the keys you want to change in a properties file. The plugin reads
`src/site/custom/project-info-reports.properties` by default; set `customBundle` to use another path:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <reporting>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-project-info-reports-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <!-- this is the default value -->
          <customBundle>${esc.d}{project.basedir}/src/site/custom/project-info-reports.properties</customBundle>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
      ...
    </plugins>
  </reporting>
  ...
</project>
```

Look up the keys in the default bundle
[project-info-reports.properties](https://github.com/apache/maven-project-info-reports-plugin/blob/master/src/main/resources/project-info-reports.properties)
(translations sit next to it in
[src/main/resources](https://github.com/apache/maven-project-info-reports-plugin/tree/master/src/main/resources)).
For example, the introduction of the Mailing Lists report is `report.mailing-lists.intro`:

```properties
report.mailing-lists.intro = These are the mailing lists that have been established for this project. For each list, there is a subscribe, unsubscribe, and an archive link.
```

A custom bundle that changes this introduction and renames two reports in the site menu:

```properties
report.mailing-lists.intro = Ask usage questions on the Users list of ${esc.d}{project.name}.
report.dependency-info.name = How to Depend on It
report.dependencies.name = Third-Party Libraries
```

**Notes:**

1. Messages can use Maven properties such as `${esc.d}{project.artifactId}`.
1. A key that is not in your custom bundle keeps its default text.
1. A report's `name` key sets its label in the site menu.
